</table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tbfnote1"><label/><p>The significant results TNF&#x0002b;488 and TNF&#x02212;859 are highlighted with a grey background.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap>). With the two sets combined, TNF&#x0002b;488A was seen in 14.9&#x00025; of controls and 28.1&#x00025; of patients (<italic>P</italic>&#x0003d;0.0012, see <xref rid="tbl4" ref-type="table">Table 4</xref> <table-wrap id="tbl4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Phenotype frequencies for combined controls, bladder cancer and melanoma patients</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="left"/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="left"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="3" align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>Controls <italic>n</italic>&#x0003d;208</bold></th><th colspan="3" align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>Patients <italic>n</italic>&#x0003d;196&#x0002f;99</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="3" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Melanoma <italic>n</italic>&#x0003d;91</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">TNF&#x0002b;488G</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">207</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">208</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">99.5&#x00025;</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">194</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">196</td><td align="center" valign="t